# Overlay: turn the local GNSS receiver on. Stack it on the defaults, which are
# already the Waveshare's — this is the product image plus a receiver, not a
# bring-up instrument:
#
#   idf.py -B build-i429 -DSDKCONFIG=build-i429/sdkconfig \
#          -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.gnsslocal" build
#
# Not stacked on sdkconfig.twatch: the T-Watch has a receiver of its own on
# different pins behind a rail, and the Kconfig symbol refuses that board
# because the navigation page and the tick that feeds this live in
# waveshare_board.cpp.
#
# The pin is not a pair to try: WAVESHARE_BOARD_RECEIVED.md's pad table, row 7,
# reads "| 7 | `RXD` | UART0 receive — **GPIO 44** |" -- this CPU's receive
# line, so a module's TX goes there and nothing here transmits. The baud is what the
# GT-U12 was MEASURED talking at on the bench (#427); a different module needs
# a different number here, not a sweep.
#
# The pin is settled and the level on it is not. H18 in
# docs/research/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md stays PARTIAL because neither bench module's
# TX idle voltage has been measured and the S3 is not 5 V tolerant. NOT
# MEASURED is the whole claim -- put a meter on the module's TX before this
# overlay's pad sees it.
CONFIG_ATTADIPA_GNSS_LOCAL=y
CONFIG_ATTADIPA_GNSS_LOCAL_RX=44
CONFIG_ATTADIPA_GNSS_LOCAL_BAUD=115200
